:"Import a key from a web service","description":"Securely upload an external customer key onto your instance using import a key from a web service \\(for example the key REST API\\). Both symmetric and asymmetric public keys can be imported into a targeted KMF cryptographic module.Configure Key Management Framework import settings before importing a key.Upload your wrapped key into a cryptographic module using the import key from web service functionality. The example uses a symmetric key. Similar steps can be used to import an asymmetric key.","locale":"en-US","canonical_url":"https://www.servicenow.com/docs/r/platform-security/platform-encryption/import-key-webservice-1.html","release":"australia","product":"Platform Encryption","classification":"platform-encryption","topic_type":"concept","last_updated":"2026-03-12","reading_time_minutes":4,"breadcrumb":["Key Management Framework","Encryption"],"tags":["#platform-security","#encryption","#columns","#attachments","#security","#type-concept"]},"task_lines":[],"tasks":{},"codeblock_ranges":[]},"smart_blocks:ServiceNowOfficialDocs/platform-security/platform-encryption/import-key-webservice-1.md#---frontmatter---": {"path":null,"last_embed":{"hash":null},"embeddings":{},"text":null,"length":0,"last_read":{"hash":"12rwuz3","at":1784561346293},"key":"ServiceNowOfficialDocs/platform-security/platform-encryption/import-key-webservice-1.md#---frontmatter---","lines":[1,20],"size":995,"outlinks":[],"class_name":"SmartBlock"},
